ZERO first software program

STAGE-0
  Empty accessible shell.
  Keyboard-only operation.
  Semantic event log.

STAGE-1
  Local document navigation.
  Headings, links, forms, lists and landmarks.

STAGE-2
  Speech and braille adapters.
  Interruptible announcements.

STAGE-3
  HTTP(S) navigation.
  No JavaScript execution requirement for the accessibility core.

STAGE-4
  Tor transport boundary.
  Connection-state announcements.

STAGE-5
  Blind end-to-end validation.
  Measure task completion, navigation steps, announcement latency,
  recovery after errors and semantic coverage.

STAGE-6
  Independent comparison against established accessible browsers/screen readers.

NO CLAIM
  Accessibility superiority is not assumed.
  It must be demonstrated on unseen tasks.
